A||N||3||Formula88||Engine Swapped Feeback-Post your experiences||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||02-16-2001||03:38 PM||||Ok, I know everyone's been talking about this swap or that swap and how great they all feel.  What I'd like to do is get as many people who've done swaps to post what they did, about how much it cost, and how satisfied you are with the performance you got.  If you have any numbers (time slips, dyno, etc) please post them.  This way we can get one thread going with enough info for people to decide how much performance/dollar each type of swap can get.  I really want to compare the 3.4, 3800SC and V8 swaps.  Also, I'm keenly interested in the 3.4TDC.  This engine seems like it was designed with the Fiero in mind, to me.  It's high tech design just screams for a Fiero to go into.  How about it people?  Let us know what you did and what you got for your trouble!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||10
Z||000001||elfiero||02-16-2001||03:58 PM||||I've done 3 swaps:<BR>1.84 cpe,3800 4spd,this car is pocket rocket<BR>around town.Lots of fun until you hit the <BR>highway,then runs out of gears.<BR>2.85GT,3800w/440T4 auto,not quite the toy the<BR>4spd was,but a nice cruiser.<BR>3.87GTloaded,TPIV8w/440T4 auto,kool factor<BR>is off the scale,unbelivibly fast,wonderful<BR>highway machine-top end is faster than you<BR>care to go!but,I'm thinkin of going to a 5spd<BR>'cause I keep eat'in the O/D automatics.<BR>OPINION;for the bucks,go with the 3800-plenty<BR>fast for 99.9%of the guys out there....||||reg||6
Z||000002||TheFiero64||02-16-2001||05:03 PM||||So far I've only done one swap. It is boring compared to some of the swaps that have been done, but The price was right. I put the 2.8 in my 88 coupe. I noticed a big gain in power from the 2.5 4 banger. I also like the exhaust note a lot better. I have it mated to the Isuzu 5 speed. It only took me a weekend. The hard part was the fuel pump  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> The rest was almost too easy.<P>I plan on more challenging swaps in the future and I will keep my PFF family posted every step of the way.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000003||lowCG||02-18-2001||01:21 PM||||I guess it really depends on what makes you tick;I have always had higher revving,European sports cars,so the TDC was a natural,along with a small list of parts needed to do the swap.<BR>Sounds great,less filling;gets 26mpg on the highway.<BR>||||reg||1
